Hello:

Recently I uploaded the sources and documentation of my callback package to 
tsx-11.mit.edu. The package consists of two programs, which enable a Linux 
box, equipped with a modem, to accept incoming calls and to process these 
calls as requests for callback. A request for a callback is then validated 
for the user name and for the requested phone number: both must be 
`allowed', as specified in configuration files of the callback package. When 
all matches, the Linux box places a return call to the remote machine, and a 
login process is started.

To get callback working, you will need the setserial package (2.0.2 or 
higher) and getty_ps (2.0.7b or higher).

